{"_id":"68fb47d4166b018f83dfc005","roadmapSlug":"swift-ui","nodeId":"UJEyJwuTiLeea6q0H9tIW","description":"# @State\n\n`@State` is a property wrapper in SwiftUI that allows you to manage the state of a view. It's used to store values that can change over time and trigger updates to the view when they do. When a property is marked with `@State`, SwiftUI automatically manages the storage and ensures that the view is re-rendered whenever the value changes, reflecting the updated data in the user interface.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"@State","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/state","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1643c"},{"type":"official","title":"Managing user interface state","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/managing-user-interface-state","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1643d"},{"type":"article","title":"What is the @State property wrapper?","url":"https://www.hackingwithswift.com/quick-start/swiftui/what-is-the-state-property-wrapper","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1643e"},{"type":"video","title":"SwiftUI - @State Property Wrapper Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=48JYBb5yJ0s","_id":"6a7f4ec1cb44947debd1643f"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-24T09:33:08.566Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:22:09.974Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/swift-ui/content/UJEyJwuTiLeea6q0H9tIW.md"}